    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.25) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing Mason Barnett, who carries a shaky 4.82 xERA, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole, making him our highest-ceiling play. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (67.10) is a top-tier start despite the risk posed by Dustin May. The combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park (+16%) and a high-leverage leadoff role pushes **Dylan Beavers** into elite territory; his speed profile remains a critical asset in our pursuit of points in the scarce SB category. **Cal Raleigh** (70.26) also provides significant value, anchored by his high base projection and a substantial +14% park factor that makes him a must-start at catcher.\n\nThe bench decision-making process was particularly tight at the middle infield and utility spots. **Kyle Karros** (47.45) nearly forced his way into the lineup, but the optimizer ultimately favored **Alex Freeland** (47.52) and **Justin Crawford** (46.89) due to slight edge fluctuations. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a strong park factor, he is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Bryan Woo. We are keeping a close eye on **Lawrence Butler** (52.29); while he carries a respectable score, he faces a daunting challenge against Daniel Espino (1.94 xERA), which heavily penalized his base projection despite his positive platoon split. All lineup assignments remain contingent on final confirmation, and owners should monitor the status of **Will Smith**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Jeremiah Jackson**, as their scores are heavily sensitive to their finalized positions in the order. Given the prevalence of \"Lineup Pending\" tags, ensure that any late-scratch adjustments account for the risk of diminished volume if **Braden Montgomery** or **Justin Crawford** are dropped to the bottom of their respective orders.",
